<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/docs/scripting" class="inline-flex items-center text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300 font-medium transition-colors group">
      <svg class="w-4 h-4 mr-2 transform group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path></svg>
      Lua Scripting Overview
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="relative">
      <div class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-500 to-indigo-600 rounded-lg blur opacity-25"></div>
      <div class="relative">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-400 via-indigo-400 to-purple-400 mb-4 tracking-tight">Management API</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
          Create, update, and manage your server-side scripts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Registering Scripts -->
    <section id="registering">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-purple-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 13h6m-3-3v6m5 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"></path></svg>
            Registration
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
            Scripts are stored per database in the <code>_scripts</code> system collection and managed through Admin-gated endpoints under
            <code>/_api/database/{db}/scripts</code>. That collection is readable but never writable by name: the endpoints below are the only way in.
            The full request and response shapes are on the <a href="/docs/api-scripting" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300">API reference</a>.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-800/30 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-purple-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mt-0">Create Script</h3>
            <div class="bg-gray-950 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 border border-white/10 overflow-x-auto">
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">POST</span> /_api/database/{db}/scripts</div>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-4 text-xs font-mono text-gray-400 bg-black/40 p-4 rounded border border-white/5 overflow-x-auto whitespace-pre">{
  "name": "greet",
  "path": "greet/:name",
  "methods": ["GET", "POST"],
  "code": "return { message = 'Hello ' .. request.params.name }",
  "description": "Say hello",
  "service": "default"
}</div>
            <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1 text-xs text-gray-400">
              <li><code class="text-purple-300">name</code>, <code class="text-purple-300">path</code>, <code class="text-purple-300">methods</code> and <code class="text-purple-300">code</code> are required. <code>:segment</code> parts of the path populate <code>request.params</code>.</li>
              <li><code class="text-purple-300">methods</code> may contain <code>"WS"</code> to register a WebSocket handler.</li>
              <li><code class="text-purple-300">service</code> defaults to <code>"default"</code>; <code class="text-purple-300">description</code> and <code class="text-purple-300">collection</code> are optional metadata.</li>
              <li>The response is <code>{ id, name, path, methods, service, created_at }</code>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-800/30 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-purple-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mt-0">List, Read, Update, Delete</h3>
            <div class="bg-gray-950 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 border border-white/10 overflow-x-auto space-y-1">
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET</span>    /_api/database/{db}/scripts</div>
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET</span>    /_api/database/{db}/scripts/{script_id}</div>
              <div><span class="text-yellow-400">PUT</span>    /_api/database/{db}/scripts/{script_id}</div>
              <div><span class="text-red-400">DELETE</span> /_api/database/{db}/scripts/{script_id}</div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-2">
              <code>PUT</code> takes the same body as create. Updating a script takes effect on the next request; there is no restart.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-800/30 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/5">
            <h3 class="text-purple-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mt-0">Invoke Script</h3>
            <div class="bg-gray-950 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 border border-white/10 overflow-x-auto">
               <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET | POST | PUT | DELETE</span> /api/{db}/{service}/{path}</div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-2">
              The database comes first, then the service, then the script's registered path, e.g. <code>GET /api/mydb/default/greet/Alice</code>.
              Query string, headers and JSON body are exposed to the script as <code>request</code>. WebSocket handlers use the same URL with <code>ws://</code>.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-2">
              A missing service answers 404, a disabled one 400, and a service with <code>require_auth</code> (the default) answers 401 to anonymous callers before the script runs.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Services -->
    <section id="services">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-emerald-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10"></path></svg>
            Services
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
            A <strong class="text-white">service</strong> is the group a script is published under: the <code>{service}</code> segment of the invocation URL.
            Services live in the <code>_services</code> system collection of each database and are what you enable, disable, protect and document as a unit.
            <strong class="text-white">A service must exist before any script under it is reachable</strong>; nothing creates <code>default</code> for you.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-800/30 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/5 mb-6">
            <h3 class="text-emerald-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mt-0">Fields</h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-300">
              <li><code class="text-emerald-300">key</code> - identifier used in URLs (<code>default</code>, <code>shop</code>, ...)</li>
              <li><code class="text-emerald-300">name</code>, <code class="text-emerald-300">description</code>, <code class="text-emerald-300">version</code> - metadata, also surfaced in the generated OpenAPI document</li>
              <li><code class="text-emerald-300">enabled</code> - when <code>false</code>, every script in the service answers 400</li>
              <li><code class="text-emerald-300">require_auth</code> - when <code>true</code> (the default), anonymous callers get 401 before any script runs</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-gray-800/30 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/5 mb-4">
            <h3 class="text-emerald-400 font-bold mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mt-0">Routes</h3>
            <div class="bg-gray-950 p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm text-gray-300 border border-white/10 overflow-x-auto space-y-1">
              <div><span class="text-green-400">POST</span>   /_api/database/{db}/services</div>
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET</span>    /_api/database/{db}/services</div>
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET</span>    /_api/database/{db}/services/{key}</div>
              <div><span class="text-yellow-400">PUT</span>    /_api/database/{db}/services/{key}</div>
              <div><span class="text-red-400">DELETE</span> /_api/database/{db}/services/{key}</div>
              <div><span class="text-blue-400">GET</span>    /_api/database/{db}/services/{key}/openapi</div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-2">
              The <code>openapi</code> route returns an OpenAPI 3 document describing every HTTP script in the service (WebSocket handlers are left out), ready for client generators.
            </p>
          </div>

          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400">
            See the dedicated <a href="/docs/scripting-services" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300">Services</a> page for versioning and organising scripts across services.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CLI Management -->
    <section id="cli">
      <div class="bg-gray-900/40 backdrop-blur-sm border border-white/10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-2xl">
        <div class="p-8 border-b border-white/5 bg-white/5">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center mt-0 border-0">
            <svg class="w-6 h-6 mr-3 text-gray-400" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 9l3 3-3 3m5 0h3M5 20h14a2 2 0 002-2V6a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z"></path></svg>
            CLI Tools
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="p-8">
          <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">
             The <code>solidb</code> binary can also sync a folder of <code>.lua</code> files with a database, mapping file paths to script paths
             (<code>users/_id.lua</code> becomes <code>users/:id</code>). Methods and metadata come from a comment header
             (<code>-- @methods GET, POST</code>, <code>-- @description</code>, <code>-- @collection</code>, <code>-- @ws</code>); the service is set once per project
             in <code>solidb-scripts.toml</code> or with <code>SOLIDB_SERVICE</code>.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 font-mono text-sm text-gray-300">
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts init</span> <span class="text-gray-500">--host localhost --port 6745 --db mydb</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts login</span> <span class="text-gray-500">-u admin</span> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts logout</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts list</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts push</span> <span class="text-gray-500">[file-or-dir]</span> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts pull</span> <span class="text-gray-500">[--force]</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts watch</span> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts diff</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts delete</span> <span class="text-gray-500">users/:id</span>
             </li>
             <li class="bg-black/20 p-2 rounded border border-white/5">
               <span class="text-green-400">solidb scripts test</span>
             </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-4">
            Full command reference on the <a href="/docs/tooling#solidb-scripts" class="text-indigo-400 hover:text-indigo-300">Tooling</a> page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
